/* heal-maladies-god.irh -- fixture for tools/check_heal_maladies.sh (bd
   inc-xr8i). Recreated after the earlier fixture of this name was deleted;
   this one is simpler.

   ONE test god. Joining it (wizard mode "Become Divine Champion") throws
   EV_BLESSING once with 30000 favour (src/Debug.cpp), and the FAVOUR_CHART
   below is copied from tools/fixtures/periodic-interval-gods.irh: its first
   rung (1000) sits under 30000 and its second (50000) sits over it, so a
   fresh follower always lands on level 1 and this handler fires exactly
   once, never again on the same character. The one-shot guard is
   getGodLevel(...)==1, the same gate periodic-interval-gods.irh uses, and it
   matters: this file's own history includes a fixture that re-afflicted the
   player every level-up and eventually died SIGSEGV.

   The blessing calls GainPermStati directly on the nine non-PARALYSIS
   maladies this check covers -- BLIND, CONFUSED, DISEASED, STUNNED,
   POISONED, HALLU, BLEEDING, CHOKING, WOUNDED -- the same call
   lib/religion.irh:5958 (Zurvash) makes from its own EV_BLESSING. PARALYSIS
   is deliberately absent: it is out of scope for inc-xr8i and stays that
   way.

   Val and Mag are pinned to 0, rather than left at their -1 default, because
   BLEEDING's per-turn pulse (src/Creature.cpp:1782-1786) reads Mag as a
   damage amount; an explicit 0 keeps a scripted character from taking
   surprise damage between the join and the cast this check is timing.

   POISONED and DISEASED name a real eID -- an existing stock Effect
   resource, $"arsenic" and $"devil chills" -- rather than GainPermStati's
   default eID of 0. Both have their own per-turn "overcome" loop
   (Creature::DoTurn's POISONED block, src/Creature.cpp:1748-1774, and
   Creature::DiseasePulse, src/Creature.cpp:1845-1884) that dereferences
   TEFF(S->eID) every turn the stati is held: unconditionally, to read the
   pulse interval, and again inside HasFlag(EF_LETHAL) on a failed save. eID
   0 names no real resource. Reading its interval field happened not to
   crash; the HasFlag read did, reproducibly, under lldb: EXC_BAD_ACCESS in
   Creature::DoTurn, address 0x3b, backtrace Game::Play -> Throw ->
   RealThrow -> ThrowEvent -> ThrowTo -> Creature::Event -> Creature::DoTurn.
   Observed 2026-09-17 while diagnosing why --prove-red's mutated run
   (maladies never cured, so the pulse keeps firing every turn until one
   fails its save) crashed where the ordinary run (cured before that
   happened) did not. Not filed as an engine defect: every real caller of
   GainPermStati(POISONED,...) or GainPermStati(DISEASED,...) already in
   lib/ names a real eID; this fixture is what had the gap, and the fix
   belongs here, not in src/.

   NOT part of the shipped module: tools/check_heal_maladies.sh splices this
   file onto the END of a scratch copy of lib/main.irc, under logs/, for the
   span of its own run only. No tracked lib/ file is ever touched. */

God "Heal Maladies Test God"
  {
    Lists:
      * FAVOUR_CHART
          1000
          50000
          60000
          70000
          80000
          90000
          100000
          110000
          120000
          130000;
    On Event EV_BLESSING {
      if (EActor->getGodLevel($"Heal Maladies Test God") == 1) {
        EActor->GainPermStati(BLIND,NULL,SS_MISC,0,0);
        EActor->GainPermStati(CONFUSED,NULL,SS_MISC,0,0);
        EActor->GainPermStati(DISEASED,NULL,SS_MISC,0,0,$"devil chills");
        EActor->GainPermStati(STUNNED,NULL,SS_MISC,0,0);
        EActor->GainPermStati(POISONED,NULL,SS_MISC,0,0,$"arsenic");
        EActor->GainPermStati(HALLU,NULL,SS_MISC,0,0);
        EActor->GainPermStati(BLEEDING,NULL,SS_MISC,0,0);
        EActor->GainPermStati(CHOKING,NULL,SS_MISC,0,0);
        EActor->GainPermStati(WOUNDED,NULL,SS_MISC,0,0);
        }
      return NOTHING;
      };
  }
